# Findings

## High — The pre-reload evidence does not exclude a stale completion message from all current output

Before `/reload`, the harness checks `reload_message` only in `recent-unwrapped`; it never captures or checks the current visible text. Readiness later accepts the message from the combination of visible and recent output. A completion message already present only in visible output could therefore satisfy the post-command poll without being proven new, contrary to the ordered work and acceptance requirement. Capture both current `visible` and `recent-unwrapped` output before submission and assert the completion text is absent from each normalized source.

## Medium — Initial protected-baseline failure can break the recovery handler

The `ERR` trap is installed before `baseline_socket` is assigned, while `set -u` remains active. If the initial `baseline_socket="$(assert_endpoint)"` fails, `recover_owned_run` calls `capture_recovery_state`, which expands the still-unbound `baseline_socket` variable and aborts recovery instead of preserving the promised endpoint/peer/media evidence. Initialize recovery-visible baseline variables before installing the trap, or provide a separate nounset-safe baseline-failure capture path.
